  "methodology": "Actual-workspace startup plus original selected-file inspection after deployment. Complete original source, reader, inventory, navigation and evidence JSON payloads compared; record retains only hashes. Both source selections reuse compilation and preserve history/candidates without restored approval. Bounded native rings have zero eviction. Collection workers retain their coordinator trace/parent. Wall intervals overlap; current-thread worker CPU does not include child-process CPU. Single workload observations, not a controlled speedup or field percentiles. Checked execution-span names: atlas.compile, atlas.project.extract, atlas.search and analysis.render.",
  "scope": "Shared application collection and native I/O adapters. No compiler-captured implementation, lexical source parser, generated wire, browser runtime or dependency change. Positive actual-tool/negative/failure/restart journeys are not new refinement, whole-app proof, live-model/cold-install, local inference or confidentiality evidence.",
  "remaining": "Generic layout, metadata-cache orchestration, observation-revision correspondence, native freshness waits, first-exposure rendering and retirement remain under the original five-step plan.",
